[[:db/retract 17592186092853 :question/answer-fields 17592186091583] {:db/id "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/d07ec1ad2b4e9e37f37261031eca01a777648504002a3ec36c9c44cf222dd555" :answer/id #uuid "e488e65f-b5f7-5848-a368-c8ad84fc3a96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/0d09a14937d6f3a3f8d622c937aa84022193e72564fcf297b93d51822d14ba03" :answer/id #uuid "db1c5ada-5a0a-5063-95fc-28435884e3e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/fda001e23440bfcd3625f4e1f6c2c484bd5ba7be9a3c8796202e5908143f553d" :answer/id #uuid "f568d7af-2838-5633-b97b-4baee3c39272" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/494364bb0608e53848d0b6ea869cfa4edde2ebb1752427a26024f97c41b9cc59" :answer/id #uuid "7e47c47d-5f99-500a-a4e9-1f25e3e802bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/4ea5f14f60294cacd7541b8ca687ce97170377e29f85c01e7d49146deeb845b9" :answer/id #uuid "0abfab4b-dab0-58b5-a000-0e2dac192e62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c" :answer-field/id #uuid "27f2d4a8-e7a5-529c-95d3-733cf6b94ace" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/d07ec1ad2b4e9e37f37261031eca01a777648504002a3ec36c9c44cf222dd555" :answer-field/choices ["q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/d07ec1ad2b4e9e37f37261031eca01a777648504002a3ec36c9c44cf222dd555" "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/0d09a14937d6f3a3f8d622c937aa84022193e72564fcf297b93d51822d14ba03" "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/fda001e23440bfcd3625f4e1f6c2c484bd5ba7be9a3c8796202e5908143f553d" "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/494364bb0608e53848d0b6ea869cfa4edde2ebb1752427a26024f97c41b9cc59" "q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c/4ea5f14f60294cacd7541b8ca687ce97170377e29f85c01e7d49146deeb845b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9384"] :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$ are the eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -7 \\\\ 14 & 11\\end{aligned}]$,\nfind two linearly independent eigenvectors of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the eigenvalues separately. \n\n- For $\\lambda =-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -7 \\\\ 14 & 11\\end{aligned}]-(-3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -7 \\\\ 14 & 14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 14{x}_{1}+14{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 14 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For $\\lambda =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -7 \\\\ 14 & 11\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 & -7 \\\\ 14 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-14{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 14{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-14 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector\n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, two linearly independent eigenvectors of the matrix $A$ are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9384/selection/ma-v1/dc4925bf38185c8014d6daec8355785587713690e4dab4ff9598725ba52da76c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789/selection/8ac02d42466f861ccee911e7657dead06f1054031678b6630f1908febe452f2a" :answer/id #uuid "a5cc9e44-6859-5b68-a7a9-7968a8266d96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789/selection/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903" :answer/id #uuid "6f3544ec-5b8e-5942-bc62-bb29bbb5a498" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789/selection/31fa59259eb049be485da4965aa54308b3447051deb89b48e73f81e0e6c7c3db" :answer/id #uuid "32891625-9574-5c20-ad26-45eb81d9ee16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789/selection/d980336960e77bdd1b51248e49daa508cfab51cd88276bbeee0ffb673c80cd39" :answer/id #uuid "04663488-c0fe-5751-b914-171cb95b56bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789/selection/6848bfa3f776003b31df52a22a1e2419b295fd5ff33cfba4f71a666383fa7366" :answer/id #uuid "c54f7555-8c95-5c25-854c-0a3f0ab36dbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c737afd-53b7-5d46-8c02-c75f15633e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36789/selection/8ac02d42466f861ccee911e7657dead06f1054031678b6630f1908febe452f2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-36789/selection/8ac02d42466f861ccee911e7657dead06f1054031678b6630f1908febe452f2a" "q-36789/selection/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903" "q-36789/selection/31fa59259eb049be485da4965aa54308b3447051deb89b48e73f81e0e6c7c3db" "q-36789/selection/d980336960e77bdd1b51248e49daa508cfab51cd88276bbeee0ffb673c80cd39" "q-36789/selection/6848bfa3f776003b31df52a22a1e2419b295fd5ff33cfba4f71a666383fa7366"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36789" :question/id #uuid "60baa1cc-5bec-5c5e-b7f7-4efe1f7a3de3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36789" :question/problem "Find an eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}16 & -30 \\\\ 9 & -17\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =-2.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & -30 \\\\ 9 & -17\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 & -30 \\\\ 9 & -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}18{x}_{1}-30{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 9{x}_{1}-15{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}18 & -30 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -15 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}18 & -30 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n18{x}_{1}-30{x}_{2}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36789/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d491b223-3526-5db0-93d1-6b08c1f7b7b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36789"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321/selection/b850599e940b61fffd431fafe2dbd1ce8f434da6657e815842d66375d23a0c0d" :answer/id #uuid "c6ee4de7-3866-5db3-a9cd-de02f8e09bf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" :answer/id #uuid "3d5d0ded-3265-5619-bf16-41e4ede36d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321/selection/b70163afa80242b6e07599db9e6649592c88c8df8d6892329736a0a5f2ef7d0f" :answer/id #uuid "05a327d7-1bc0-58e4-bd27-d8a4e6d43c12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321/selection/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" :answer/id #uuid "a294065b-c5ec-524d-bb38-66b44adbc4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321/selection/fa3f23c7334055936c2275cd39a879c618af1144bc7e7a75445f0ec46dcc7115" :answer/id #uuid "f910e73c-fa87-506e-ba75-9aad70290256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d3813a1-03d2-54af-8c13-95d5b91e3efb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80321/selection/b70163afa80242b6e07599db9e6649592c88c8df8d6892329736a0a5f2ef7d0f" :answer-field/choices ["q-80321/selection/b850599e940b61fffd431fafe2dbd1ce8f434da6657e815842d66375d23a0c0d" "q-80321/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" "q-80321/selection/b70163afa80242b6e07599db9e6649592c88c8df8d6892329736a0a5f2ef7d0f" "q-80321/selection/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" "q-80321/selection/fa3f23c7334055936c2275cd39a879c618af1144bc7e7a75445f0ec46dcc7115"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80321" :question/id #uuid "66d09f18-29eb-5ec8-ac1c-91dd52fe0ddf" :question/math-academy-id "q-80321" :question/problem "Find an eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =-2.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d491b223-3526-5db0-93d1-6b08c1f7b7b5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305/selection/2cdfcf71c4e9f37094558e0bc731bba5c7d82fe006ad1ed5408b9a83d298bede" :answer/id #uuid "8d64319a-65c6-54c6-b54d-31b2fecf1c8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305/selection/4e8a2b6c0dfdcec910a08dc5fcfec3e20024a9ff0f21c0321f253f62dd775d55" :answer/id #uuid "f329ad93-2dbf-5e79-9617-16ebf04d2153" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305/selection/0a0cc3e9067c88c2c988cea3d7f98535fcefb811f9365842c3f000e05bbd5f80" :answer/id #uuid "5d23617a-dd03-581c-8b85-ce542f2cb7ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305/selection/385203d12ab40a6a4c93e93d2dc3cb994e957ac457c360ff3baee07903252b0d" :answer/id #uuid "79d91e49-5246-52ce-ac59-216094121dce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305/selection/1532499c2f02261801c221b62381830809decaa35ec20a536577c2777ed2628a" :answer/id #uuid "66ee4a47-d037-5279-bc33-8f70eabf8d13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c59e680-ab27-5a9f-a27b-cde02e0e89f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107305/selection/2cdfcf71c4e9f37094558e0bc731bba5c7d82fe006ad1ed5408b9a83d298bede" :answer-field/choices ["q-107305/selection/2cdfcf71c4e9f37094558e0bc731bba5c7d82fe006ad1ed5408b9a83d298bede" "q-107305/selection/4e8a2b6c0dfdcec910a08dc5fcfec3e20024a9ff0f21c0321f253f62dd775d55" "q-107305/selection/0a0cc3e9067c88c2c988cea3d7f98535fcefb811f9365842c3f000e05bbd5f80" "q-107305/selection/385203d12ab40a6a4c93e93d2dc3cb994e957ac457c360ff3baee07903252b0d" "q-107305/selection/1532499c2f02261801c221b62381830809decaa35ec20a536577c2777ed2628a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107305" :question/id #uuid "012179b2-c89e-5745-a680-f7f5cfa0c196" :question/math-academy-id "q-107305" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =10$ are the eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$,\nfind two linearly independent eigenvectors of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the eigenvalues separately. \n\n- For $\\lambda =3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain  ${x}_{1}=-3{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For $\\lambda =10,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}]-10[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, two linearly independent eigenvectors of the matrix $A$ are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-107305/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "022c4cb4-d6f6-56a5-a6dc-3adfc5aabda7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107305"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008/selection/12e6badc02b8b2e3e0ffeef9846df1ac2f078fb0f8b831a62b9a519b01cf928f" :answer/id #uuid "6493921c-3b28-567d-b8c6-59d4d06908b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008/selection/fbb8517d1e4aa789bfaaed63fcf9c79bd62b573b5579e8f279d70bf62f481269" :answer/id #uuid "a843e8ac-955c-5dd7-8ffa-b5521f37db1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008/selection/9d8eca1559bd42b44b8a8d3f9c651f7ccbf931686da787b7ba05e011ff8d3e95" :answer/id #uuid "60554852-fcea-57a9-901b-9fa88172485e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008/selection/a4d5687a4b3db94429e83c952e8339f8c92f4cfbd07ff12ab8681dbd93cbf466" :answer/id #uuid "bf5d6b71-b970-5ec8-bff0-167e4bba82c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008/selection/5becdd897ff339c86c51dea7070e605a914d5b4e8cb4a53a2100018f864fa6c8" :answer/id #uuid "014cff4f-292e-5bda-92c0-012532db1031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fad4f090-a9e7-579a-8701-46f2afd0ca0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108008/selection/12e6badc02b8b2e3e0ffeef9846df1ac2f078fb0f8b831a62b9a519b01cf928f" :answer-field/choices ["q-108008/selection/12e6badc02b8b2e3e0ffeef9846df1ac2f078fb0f8b831a62b9a519b01cf928f" "q-108008/selection/fbb8517d1e4aa789bfaaed63fcf9c79bd62b573b5579e8f279d70bf62f481269" "q-108008/selection/9d8eca1559bd42b44b8a8d3f9c651f7ccbf931686da787b7ba05e011ff8d3e95" "q-108008/selection/a4d5687a4b3db94429e83c952e8339f8c92f4cfbd07ff12ab8681dbd93cbf466" "q-108008/selection/5becdd897ff339c86c51dea7070e605a914d5b4e8cb4a53a2100018f864fa6c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108008" :question/id #uuid "1fd83815-31c4-57cb-8ceb-4b7d6dee8403" :question/math-academy-id "q-108008" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =6$ are the eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$,\nfind two linearly independent eigenvectors of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the eigenvalues separately. \n\n- For $\\lambda =-5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]-(-5)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{2}{9}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain  ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For $\\lambda =6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, two linearly independent eigenvectors of the matrix $A$ are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108008/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "022c4cb4-d6f6-56a5-a6dc-3adfc5aabda7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108008"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
